Varargs (variable arguments): allows a method to accept zero or more arguments of the same type.

Syntax: type... paramName  (must be the LAST parameter)

public int sum(int... numbers) {
    int total = 0;
    for (int n : numbers) total += n;
    return total;
}

// Can call with any number of args:
sum()           // → 0
sum(1)          // → 1
sum(1, 2, 3)    // → 6
sum(1, 2, 3, 4) // → 10

Under the hood: varargs is just an array.
Only ONE varargs param allowed per method; must be last.

